  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Vigor Marine has federal contract obligations of $699M in FY2026 to date. The company received 29 awards this fiscal year to date, with an average award size of $24.1M and obligations up 57.4% year over year. Department of Defense is the dominant buyer, obligating $664M, followed by Department of Homeland Security with $34M and Department of Transportation with $1.5M. Ship Building and Repairing is the largest market for federal work, accounting for $698M, while Other Support Activities for Water Transportation accounts for $1.5M and Steam and Air-Conditioning Supply accounts for $2.8K. Historical obligations show a rising profile beginning at $304M in FY21, moving to $353M in FY22, $309M in FY23, $448M in FY24, $444M in FY25, and $699M in FY26. Current-year totals are partial because the fiscal year is ongoing, and the note clarifies that listed award-value figures in largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables are total contract values rather than current-year obligations.",
